A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate only when evidence supports the **same cause** as an open ticket
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-triage-by-cause), replacing the subject-only rule):

1. Read the body and look up the tenant's locale and booking-form version.
2. Check the input channel and compare causes using the shared logic in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`.
3. Merge supported duplicates; keep different causes apart. Investigate unknown tenants and unexplained symptoms before merging.

<Callout>
Subjects and browser-language intake tags are clues, not proof of the cause. Different causes can
share a subject; the same cause can arrive under different subjects.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep the report separate until you can establish the failing path. Preserve its body and tenant
details so engineering can investigate. An unknown tenant does not prove a new cause.
